<task id="004" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-02: App-only agreement classify + edit-plan Action behind a new PublicContracts facade (IAgreementAi / AgreementAi / NullAgreementAi), schema-valid edit plans on 3 synthetic NDAs</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations and cleanup</phase>
    <gate>blocked — external PR #3163 (edit-plan.schema.json, topics.yaml, synthetic corpus on master) and task 005 (ConsumerTypes constants)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds .cs code to the BFF (new facade + Null peer + DI registrations) and a new catalogued Action; tags include bff-api and ai.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single-component facade with an exact reference to copy (IInvoiceAi / InvoiceAi / NullInvoiceAi) and existing JPS skills for the Action.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P0-A2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>005</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, azure-openai, di, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Give the BFF an app-only way to (1) classify an agreement with the existing `agreement-classify` Action and (2) produce an accelerator edit plan for an NDA, through a new PublicContracts facade on the IInvoiceAi pattern. The edit plan must validate against the accelerator's `edit-plan.schema.json`, with every `topic` id present in the pinned NDA `topics.yaml` (v1.2).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the JPS Action catalogue (Actions, Bindings, ConsumerTypes), the PublicContracts AI facade boundary and .NET 10 Minimal API DI. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`IAgreementAi` (ClassifyAsync, BuildEditPlanAsync) with `AgreementAi` (IActionResolver + IActionRunner by ConsumerTypes key, fail closed) and `NullAgreementAi` (ADR-032 P3), registered in AnalysisServicesModule beside IInvoiceAi; a new catalogued Action `agreement-edit-plan` (action JSON + input/output schema + Binding row + `ConsumerTypes.AgreementEditPlan` in `All`); unit tests proving schema-valid plans on the 3 synthetic NDAs and a not-an-NDA result on the synthetic MSA.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-02 (acceptance a–d), NFR-09 (pinned standard version), NFR-10. `agreement-classify` and `agreement-review` already exist (`infra/dataverse/actions/*.action.json`). `agreement-review`'s output is a CLOSED contract (`{overallRisk, flaggedSections[]}`) consumed by the Console review flow (`src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/useAgreementReviewGate.ts`, memo and Word-comment export), so it is NOT changed: the edit plan comes from a new Action whose output schema mirrors `edit-plan.schema.json`'s `edits` shape. The facade fills `author`, `date`, `review_basis` (standard name + pinned version) and `provenance` deterministically; the model produces only topic-keyed edits. Task 005 adds the `agreement-classify` / `nda-review` / `nda-standard-summary` constants (FR-03 item 6, which also satisfies FR-02(d)); this task adds only `AgreementEditPlan`.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IAgreementAi.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/AgreementAi.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/NullAgreementAi.cs</file>
      <file role="new">infra/dataverse/actions/agreement-edit-plan.action.json</file>
