  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm #3163 and 005 are merged; read edit-plan.schema.json and topics.yaml on master.</step>
    <step order="2">Author `agreement-edit-plan` with `/jps-action-create` (input: document text + standard topics; output: Structured-Outputs-compatible `edits[]` mirroring the schema's edit item); validate with `/jps-validate`.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the Binding row and `ConsumerTypes.AgreementEditPlan` (+ `All`).</step>
    <step order="4">Write IAgreementAi / AgreementAi / NullAgreementAi copying the InvoiceAi shape; ClassifyAsync maps agreement-classify output (isAgreement, candidates, confidence); BuildEditPlanAsync assembles the full plan (deterministic header fields + model edits) and validates it against the schema and topic list before returning; invalid → typed failure, never a partial plan.</step>
    <step order="5">Register in AnalysisServicesModule (Null unconditional, real in AddPublicContractsFacade).</step>
    <step order="6">Write AgreementAiTests (mocked IActionRunner outputs recorded from the synthetic corpus) and run the catalog drift test (`RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheckTests`).</step>
    <step order="7">Run a dev smoke of the real Action on the 3 synthetic NDAs + the MSA only if the owner OKs a dev Action deploy; otherwise record that 008 does it.</step>
    <step order="8">`dotnet build`, `dotnet test`; measure publish size vs fresh master.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations in `projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If producing an edit plan appears to require changing `agreement-review`'s output contract (instead of the new `agreement-edit-plan` Action), STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 — it breaks Console consumers.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the edit-plan schema cannot be expressed in Azure OpenAI Structured Outputs (e.g. `format`, `oneOf`), keep model output to the compatible subset and validate the full plan in code; if even `edits[]` cannot be expressed, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>Deploying the Action/Binding to dev needs the owner's OK (project CLAUDE.md §5).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>reuse-scan.md row 14 (app-only AI Action from code): `AppOnlyAnalysisService.cs:545`, `InvoiceAi.cs:30`; verdict "new PublicContracts facade for agreement Actions, on the InvoiceAi pattern". CAPABILITY-INDEX row 17 (let another BFF module use AI). The `agreement-edit-plan` Action has no existing equivalent: `agreement-review` emits findings, not an edit plan.</existing>
    <extension>No — `IInvoiceAi` is invoice-typed and owned by ebilling-r1 (frozen until UAT); `agreement-review`'s closed output contract is consumed by the Console and cannot carry a plan.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The NDA harness (task 015) has no edit plan to hand the engines, so no marked-up NDA is produced server-side (FR-02, FR-09 fail).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
  </tools>

