  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each of the 3 synthetic NDAs, BuildEditPlanAsync returns a plan that validates against `edit-plan.schema.json` (JsonSchema.Net) and every `topic` id exists in the pinned `topics.yaml` (FR-02a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The plan's `review_basis` names "Spaarke NDA – Mutual" and the pinned version v1.2 (NFR-09).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given the synthetic MSA, ClassifyAsync reports not-an-NDA and no plan is built (FR-02b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a model output with an unknown topic id or a schema violation yields a typed failure, never a returned plan.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with AI off, `NullAgreementAi` throws its typed exception; DI resolves `IAgreementAi` in both modes (DiGraphValidationTests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ConsumerTypes.All` contains `agreement-edit-plan`, the Binding row exists, and RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheckTests report no drift (FR-02d with task 005).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`agreement-review.action.json`, `agreement-classify.action.json` and their Binding rows are byte-unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No test reads `answer-key/` or a real NDA (FR-02c, NFR-10).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PR states Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB total, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Brief deviation: the main session listed deps "none"; this task depends on 005 because both edit ConsumerTypes.cs (file overlap, task-create Step 3.8) and on external #3163 for the schema/corpus. Facade naming (`IAgreementAi`) is a proposal; keep it if no closer name exists in PublicContracts. Deterministic anchoring (owner 2026-11-26, notes/decisions.md): segment_clauses runs first (engine job `segment` operation); the edit-plan AI picks `para` only from the closed para_key list and quotes verbatim; the BFF exact-match pre-check refuses bad anchors (closed codes) before the engine; never fuzzy, approximate or whole-document text matching. This task: Action input = segment_clauses JSON (not free text); para constrained to supplied keys; exact-match pre-check with negative tests (FR-02e).</notes>

